# Hand-authored (NOT produced by genextra.py).
# PROBE for a regARIMA design and an x11regression{} design in the SAME run --
# the pairing behind xrgdrv's `Ncusrx == 0` support guard, and the one that four
# separate stand-ins had never had to survive.
#
# Body is generated/airline_user-reg-x11 (two user regressors) plus a plain
# x11regression{ variables=(td) }. That single block promotes Ixreg to 2
# (gtinpt.f:1201, Lmodel), which turns on xrgdrv's transparent prior-TD pass --
# and the transparent pass runs BEFORE the regARIMA estimate, so anything it
# leaves behind lands in the model.
#
# What it gates:
#   * gtinpt.f:804/832's ssprep/restor of the DESIGN. Parsing x11regression{}
#     builds into the working model arrays; without the restore the regression{}
#     columns are simply gone (nreg: 0 against the oracle's 2).
#   * xrgdrv.f:207's restor, same field set, one phase later.
#   * xrgdrv.f:66-74/225-231's ubkx backup of the user MATRIX itself.
#   * x11pt2.f:851-859's six per-factor divsubs in the x11reg Stcsi rebuild --
#     Adjusr is 1 here, which is what makes the Facusr one live.
#   * x11pt2.f:284-290's Adjcyc arm being print-only: Adjcyc is 1 for this whole
#     window (chkadj runs at arima.f:1256, AFTER xrgdrv) on any spec that has a
#     regression{} spec at all, so a refusal keyed on it fired here.
series{
  title  = "Intl Airline Passengers"
  file   = "../data/airline.dat"
  start  = 1949.01
  period = 12
  save   = (b1)
}
transform{
  function = log
}
regression{
